# TuneSlap Project Structure

## Repository Overview
The TuneSlap project is a monorepo containing the unified frontend application and backend services:

```
tuneslap/
├── frontend/           # Unified web application (Next.js)
├── server/            # Go backend API
├── infra/             # Terraform infrastructure
├── openapi/           # API documentation
└── scripts/           # Development scripts
```

## Frontend Structure
The frontend is a Next.js App Router application containing both marketing pages and the main application:

```
frontend/
├── app/                  # App Router pages and layouts
│   ├── (authenticated)/  # Protected application routes (dashboard, library)
│   ├── (index)/         # Marketing landing pages
│   ├── auth/            # Authentication routes
│   ├── api/             # API routes
│   └── globals.css      # Global styles
├── components/           # Reusable components
├── contexts/            # Global state contexts
├── hooks/               # Custom hooks
├── utils/               # Utility functions
└── public/              # Static assets
```

## Development Workflow

### Package Management
- **Always use Yarn** for the frontend
- Never mix package managers (remove package-lock.json if present)
- Use `yarn add` for new dependencies
- Use `yarn dev` for development server

### File Naming Conventions
- **Components**: PascalCase (e.g., `Header.tsx`, `Footer.tsx`)
- **Pages**: lowercase with hyphens (e.g., `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`)
- **Utilities**: camelCase (e.g., `utils.ts`)
- **Types**: PascalCase with `.types.ts` suffix

### Import Paths
Use absolute imports with the `@/` alias:
- `@/components/EmptyState` - Components
- `@/hooks/useAuth` - Custom hooks
- `@/utils/helpers` - Utility functions
- `@/app/globals.css` - Global styles

## Content Management

### Marketing Content
Marketing content is managed within the `app/(index)` components (e.g., `Hero.tsx`, `Features.tsx`).

### SEO and Metadata
- Update metadata in `app/layout.tsx` for global SEO
- Add page-specific metadata for each route
- Use proper Open Graph tags for social sharing
- Include relevant keywords for search optimization

## Infrastructure

### Deployment
- Frontend deploys to `tuneslap.com`
- Use Terraform configurations in `infra/` for infrastructure
- Separate staging and production environments

### Environment Management
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Keep sensitive data out of version control
- Use different configs for staging vs production

## Quality Standards

### Code Quality
- Use TypeScript for type safety
- Follow ESLint configuration
- Use Prettier for code formatting
- Write semantic, accessible HTML

### Performance
- Optimize images with Next.js Image component
- Use proper loading states and error boundaries
- Implement code splitting for better performance
- Monitor Core Web Vitals

### Accessibility
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Include proper ARIA labels
- Ensure keyboard navigation works
- Maintain proper color contrast ratios
